 "plan": {
  "angle": "A restaurant site already carries the menu, the hours and the address; a restaurant landing page does one job that the site does badly, such as a large-party request, a catering quote, a ticketed holiday dinner or a list for a new location. This page shows four of those pages with the form, the rule behind it and the row each request leaves in a database the owner keeps, then gives seven build steps an owner or general manager can follow. It makes no health-code, liquor, payment or delivery-platform claims, and the wedding sibling stays out of the headings.",
  "tab_stories": [
   "Peppervine Bistro asks for party size first; a request for 8 or more guests emails events manager Rosalind Haddix instead of offering a table time, and of 64 requests this week 9 went to her and 55 picked a time.",
   "Stonewick Smokehouse takes catering requests with the date, the guest count and pickup or delivery; every order for 50 or more guests goes to catering lead Teo Beaty, and this month he got 12 of 31 requests while 19 went to the kitchen.",
   "Lark Hollow Tavern sells 40 seats for a $95 New Year's Eve tasting menu; once 40 seats are reserved the form takes waitlist names instead, and 14 people have joined the waitlist.",
   "Sartino's Pizzeria is opening a second location in Westvale and asks each signup which location they would visit; of 212 signups, 138 picked Westvale and get the opening-night invite, and 74 picked Downtown."
  ],
